  "overview": "**Skyline** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#de175c` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Open Sans` (41px display down to 14px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Benevity**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://skyline.benevity.org/). Inventory: **16** colors, **50** typography steps, and **50** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 50 component tokens with documented paddings: `4px 8px`, `20px`, `5px 9px`, `16px`, `.5rem 1.0714285714rem`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#fafafa` cards; separate sibling sections using `#e0e0e0` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 2px 4px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.06)`, `0 2px 4px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.06)`) paired with `#e0e0e0` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#de175c` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#de175c` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.5:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Open Sans` headings with `Open Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (4px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#fafafa` surface shifts and `#e0e0e0` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `sky-date-input` fields and secondary buttons."
